From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: define GetCache out of line, after Device

PipelineStateCacheKeyComponent<Key>::GetCache accesses m_parentDevice,
whose type Device is only forward-declared at PipelineStateCache.hpp's
point in the pch.hpp include order; device.hpp comes twelve includes
later. The body calls a member template on that incomplete type.

MSVC accepts this because it defers the dependent member access until
instantiation, by which point Device is complete. Clang binds the
non-dependent parts of a template body when the template is parsed, so
it reports "member access into incomplete type 'Device'" -- and then,
because it cannot see the member, rejects the disambiguating 'template'
keyword too. Both errors have one cause.

Moving the definition to the end of device.hpp, after Device is defined,
is the minimal fix: the body is unchanged and the declaration stays where
it was, so nothing about the class's interface or instantiation behavior
moves. The 'template' disambiguator is retained -- it is still a
dependent member template call, and MSVC accepts it in this position.
---
diff --git a/include/PipelineStateCache.hpp b/include/PipelineStateCache.hpp
index 004d188..9c1ce4a 100644
--- a/include/PipelineStateCache.hpp
+++ b/include/PipelineStateCache.hpp
@@ -127,10 +127,7 @@ namespace D3D11On12
     {
         using CacheEntry = PipelineStateCacheEntry<Key>;
         std::vector<std::weak_ptr<CacheEntry>> m_pPSOComponents;
-        PipelineStateCacheLocked<Key> GetCache()
-        {
-            return m_parentDevice.template GetPSOCache<Key>();
-        }
+        PipelineStateCacheLocked<Key> GetCache();
 
         // Immovable
         PipelineStateCacheKeyComponent(Device& device)
diff --git a/include/device.hpp b/include/device.hpp
index a4eeb2c..a2d2894 100644
--- a/include/device.hpp
+++ b/include/device.hpp
@@ -628,4 +628,15 @@ namespace D3D11On12
         UINT m_ExecutionCount = 0;
         bool m_bMapDiscardCalled;
     };
+
+    // Defined out of line: at PipelineStateCache.hpp's point in pch.hpp
+    // Device is only forward-declared, and this body needs it complete.
+    // MSVC accepts the in-class body because it defers the dependent
+    // member access to instantiation; Clang binds it when the template
+    // is parsed, which only works after Device is defined above.
+    template <typename Key>
+    PipelineStateCacheLocked<Key> PipelineStateCacheKeyComponent<Key>::GetCache()
+    {
+        return m_parentDevice.template GetPSOCache<Key>();
+    }
 };
